From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vh266: bound slice segment index to SLICE_MAX_NUM

Picture.slices[] is a fixed array of SLICE_MAX_NUM (= 1000) Slice pointers,
but m_uiSliceSegmentIdx is never bounded against it, and the upstream VTM
CHECK() guards are inert here (CHECK(a,b) expands to nothing). A malformed
stream with more than 1000 slice segments in one picture walks the index past
the array: index 1000 aliases the AML-added buf_cfg field, and beyond that
the accesses leave the malloc(sizeof(Picture)) allocation - a stream-driven
out-of-bounds kernel heap read and write.

xDecodeSlice() now returns -1 on the non-first-slice path once the index has
reached SLICE_MAX_NUM, ahead of every unguarded slices[] access; 0..999 still
pass, the most slices any VVC level permits. It stops the overflow but does
not reset the index, so such a stream keeps failing slices until the instance
is torn down. Only S7D (S905X5) has VVC hardware, so this is inert on g12b;
not exercised on S905X5 hardware - none available here.

--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h266/h266_bufmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h266/h266_bufmgr.c
@@ -2978,6 +2978,13 @@
 	if (p_declib->m_bFirstSliceInPicture) {
 		p_declib->m_uiSliceSegmentIdx = 0;
 	} else {
+		/* Picture.slices[] holds SLICE_MAX_NUM entries */
+		if (p_declib->m_uiSliceSegmentIdx >= SLICE_MAX_NUM) {
+			hevc_print(p_declib->hw, H266_DEBUG_BUFMGR,
+				"Err: slice segment idx %u exceeds %d slices per picture\n",
+				p_declib->m_uiSliceSegmentIdx, SLICE_MAX_NUM);
+			return -1;
+		}
 		//CHECK(nalu.m_nalUnitType != m_pcPic->slices[m_uiSliceSegmentIdx - 1]->m_eNalUnitType && !m_pcPic->cs->pps->m_mixedNaluTypesInPicFlag, "If pps_mixed_nalu_types_in_pic_flag is equal to 0, the value of NAL unit type shall be the same for all coded slice NAL units of a picture");
 		copySliceInfo(p_declib->m_apcSlicePilot, p_declib->m_pcPic->slices[p_declib->m_uiSliceSegmentIdx-1], true);
 	}
